{
  "title": "LLB (Law)",
  "kicker": "Undergraduate law degree",
  "status": "published",
  "blocks": [
    {
      "discriminant": "text",
      "value": {
        "body": "A law degree, in two forms: a five-year integrated programme straight after Class 12 (BA LLB, BBA LLB, B.Com LLB and others), or a three-year LLB after any bachelor's degree. Both are regulated by the Bar Council of India and lead to practice, corporate legal work, the judiciary or further study."
      }
    },
